{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-86608" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $z=5(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ))$ in the form $z=x+\\text{i}y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978069/state.json" "file_sha256" "1508a11256c88c65d841c696945663f7f1cdf4e5b1de2b7f6f358486951340a2"} {"question" "q-86608" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To express the number in Cartesian form, we expand the parentheses and substitute the values of the cosine and sine.\n\nSince $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )=-1$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =5(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )) \\\\  & =5(-1+\\text{i}\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978069/state.json" "file_sha256" "1508a11256c88c65d841c696945663f7f1cdf4e5b1de2b7f6f358486951340a2"} {"question" "q-86608" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978069/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3c1bf3d8a1d050d44d7529fa9ef3fa3b7f33f7d0f3396b3a91a9918da48ba822"} {"question" "q-86608" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978069/state.json" "file_sha256" "1508a11256c88c65d841c696945663f7f1cdf4e5b1de2b7f6f358486951340a2"} {"question" "q-86608" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-5"] ["math" "-5+5\\text{i}"] ["math" "-5\\text{i}"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "5+5\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978069/state.json" "file_sha256" "1508a11256c88c65d841c696945663f7f1cdf4e5b1de2b7f6f358486951340a2"} {"question" "q-86608" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978069/state.json" "file_sha256" "1508a11256c88c65d841c696945663f7f1cdf4e5b1de2b7f6f358486951340a2"} {"question" "q-107478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $z=\\frac{4}{1-\\text{i}}$ in the form $r(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978069/state.json" "file_sha256" "1508a11256c88c65d841c696945663f7f1cdf4e5b1de2b7f6f358486951340a2"} {"question" "q-107478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we express the given complex number in the form $z=x+y\\text{i}.$ To do this, we remove $\\text{i}$ from the denominator by multiplying the numerator and denominator of $z$ by the complex conjugate of the denominator, which is $1+\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{4}{1-\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4(1+\\text{i})}{(1-\\text{i})(1+\\text{i})} \\\\  & =\\frac{4(1+\\text{i})}{{1}^{2}-{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4(1+\\text{i})}{1+1} \\\\  & =2(1+\\text{i}) \\\\  & =2+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nIn polar form, $r$ represents the magnitude $|z|.$ For a complex number $z=x+y\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSo, for $z=2+2\\text{i},$ the magnitude is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nIn polar form, $\\theta $  represents the argument $\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z).$ Since $x=2$ and $y=2$ are both positive, $z$ lies in the first quadrant. So, we can find $\\theta $ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{2}{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡1 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the complex number $z$ in polar form:\n\n$$\nz=2\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}))\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978069/state.json" "file_sha256" "1508a11256c88c65d841c696945663f7f1cdf4e5b1de2b7f6f358486951340a2"} {"question" "q-107478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978069/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3c1bf3d8a1d050d44d7529fa9ef3fa3b7f33f7d0f3396b3a91a9918da48ba822"} {"question" "q-107478" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978069/state.json" "file_sha256" "1508a11256c88c65d841c696945663f7f1cdf4e5b1de2b7f6f358486951340a2"} {"question" "q-107478" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "z=2\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}))"] ["math" "z=2\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}))"] ["math" "z=4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}))"] ["math" "z=\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}))"] ["math" "z=\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}))"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978069/state.json" "file_sha256" "1508a11256c88c65d841c696945663f7f1cdf4e5b1de2b7f6f358486951340a2"} {"question" "q-107478" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "z=2\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}))"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978069/state.json" "file_sha256" "1508a11256c88c65d841c696945663f7f1cdf4e5b1de2b7f6f358486951340a2"} {"question" "q-107550" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $z=\\frac{2\\text{i}}{1+\\text{i}}$ in the form $r(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978069/state.json" "file_sha256" "1508a11256c88c65d841c696945663f7f1cdf4e5b1de2b7f6f358486951340a2"} {"question" "q-107550" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we express the given complex number in the form $z=x+y\\text{i}.$ To do this, we remove $\\text{i}$ from the denominator by multiplying the numerator and denominator of $z$ by the complex conjugate of the denominator, which is $1-\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{2\\text{i}}{1+\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\text{i}(1-\\text{i})}{(1+\\text{i})(1-\\text{i})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\text{i}-2{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{1}^{2}-{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\text{i}+2}{1+1} \\\\  & =1+\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn polar form, $r$ represents the magnitude $|z|.$ For a complex number $z=x+y\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSo, for $z=1+\\text{i},$ the magnitude is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn polar form, $\\theta $  represents the argument $\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z).$ Since $x=1$ and $y=1$ are both positive, $z$ lies in the first quadrant. So, we can find $\\theta $ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{1}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡1 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the complex number $z$ in polar form:\n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}))\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978069/state.json" "file_sha256" "1508a11256c88c65d841c696945663f7f1cdf4e5b1de2b7f6f358486951340a2"} {"question" "q-107550" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978069/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3c1bf3d8a1d050d44d7529fa9ef3fa3b7f33f7d0f3396b3a91a9918da48ba822"} {"question" "q-107550" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978069/state.json" "file_sha256" "1508a11256c88c65d841c696945663f7f1cdf4e5b1de2b7f6f358486951340a2"} {"question" "q-107550" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "z=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})"] ["math" "z=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})"] ["math" "z=\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}))"] ["math" "z=\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{4}))"] ["math" "z=\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}))"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Co